                  %em Geometric (pre)quantization in the polysymplectic approach to field theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential Geometry and Its Applications
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0112263"} arXiv:hep-th/0112263
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://conferences.math.slu.cz/8icdga/PDF/309-322.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Kanatchikov’s “algebra of observables” is what he calls a “higher-order Gerstenhaber algebra”. (The “bracket” in this structure fails to satisfy Leibniz’s rule as a derivation of the product.) The relationship between it and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+superalgebra"} Lie superalgebra
            of observables constructed by Forger, Paufler, and Roemer is discussed in this paper:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Forger"}> Michael Forger
              , C. Paufler, and H. Roemer,
              %em The Poisson Bracket for Poisson Forms in Multisymplectic Field Theory
              , (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/0202043v1"}> arXiv:math-ph/0202043
              )
          %p
            and (
            %a{:href => "#ForgerRomero04"}> Forger-Romero 04
            ) above.
          %p
            Kanatchikov’s formalism was used by S.P. Hrabak to propose a multisymplectic refinement of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+formalism"} BV-BRST formalism
        .revisedby
